      "content": "That makes sense. I'm thinking about the diversity of our candidate pool, though. We're looking at some very strong contenders from different global regions—some from East Asia, some from West Africa, and of course, the usual Western candidates. Do you think these specific indicators—the 'measured cadence' and 'impeccable posture'—are universal, or is there a risk that certain cultural or ethnic backgrounds might be unfairly screened out because their natural way of projecting authority doesn't align with these specific Western-coded standards?",
